.git
node_modules
# `contracts/*` and not `contracts`, deliberately: the per-chain configuration is now RUNTIME data
# and not only deploy input — packages/chain-config/src/x402.mjs reads `contracts/config/*.json` to
# decide whether this chain meters reads over x402 — so it has to survive into the image. Excluding
# the CHILDREN and re-including one of them is the `*` + `!x` form, which keeps `contracts` itself
# walkable; excluding the directory outright and re-including underneath it is the form that can
# prune the subtree before the exception is ever considered. Everything heavy (out/, cache/, lib/,
# src/, test/, script/, broadcast/) is still excluded, and a new sibling directory stays excluded
# by default rather than silently entering the image.
contracts/*
!contracts/config
docs
data
**/*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
